    {
      "title": "1. The Credentialing Lifecycle",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every defensible certification program follows this sequence:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#1-the-credentialing-lifecycle",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Skipping any step creates a defensibility gap under accreditation review. NCCA Standard 14 requires",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#1-the-credentialing-lifecycle",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "documented JTA linkage to every content domain in the blueprint.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#1-the-credentialing-lifecycle",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Assessment Blueprint / Test Specifications",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The blueprint (also called a table of specifications or content outline) is the governing document",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "for all item development. It must be empirically traceable to the JTA.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Blueprint architecture rules (CEDMA guidance):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No more than 7 major content domains and 20–22 total objectives",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No single objective should be assessed by only one item (minimum 3–4 items per objective)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Weight domains proportionally to JTA frequency × importance ratings",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Freeze the blueprint before item development begins; mid-cycle revisions invalidate items",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cognitive level distribution by certification tier:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Biggs's constructive alignment principle: intended learning outcomes define assessment tasks; tasks",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "define instructional activities - not the reverse.[^biggs1999] The scenario-removal test: if a candidate can",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cover the scenario and answer from the stem alone, the item is testing recall, not reasoning,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "regardless of blueprint labeling.[^cedma]",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#2-assessment-blueprint-test-specifications",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Item Writing: Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "See references/item-writing-and-psychometrics.md for full distractor analysis tables.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Well-formed stem rules:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Complete problem statement in the stem; candidates should not need to read options to understand the question",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use positive phrasing; reserve EXCEPT/NOT stems for cases where the negative is the exact professional skill being tested",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "One clear question per stem (no double-barreled constructions)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid window-dressing text that adds length without adding discriminating information",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Distractor design rules:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "All distractors must be plausible to a candidate lacking the target knowledge",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Options must be parallel in grammatical form and similar in length",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A nonfunctional distractor (selected by <5% of examinees) degrades item discrimination; flag for revision after each administration",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Never use \"all of the above\" (rewards partial knowledge) or \"none of the above\" (unless an exact answer is required, e.g., mathematical calculations)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Six flaw categories to eliminate:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Structured faculty training + peer review reduces total item flaw rates from ~67% to ~21% within",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "three years (longitudinal medical education data).[^pmc3809311]",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#3-item-writing-multiple-choice-questions-mcqs",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Performance-Based Assessment (PBA) Items",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "PBAs assess execution, not knowledge recall. Action-verb alignment rule:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Blueprint verbs \"configure,\" \"demonstrate,\" \"troubleshoot\" → hands-on lab / PBA items",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Blueprint verbs \"explain,\" \"identify,\" \"describe\" → MCQ or scenario-based items",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Mixing these creates construct-irrelevant variance",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Six-step PBA design process:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Ground each task in a specific JTA task statement",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Define scoring criteria (success outcomes) before designing the environment",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Engage SMEs during design, not as final reviewers only",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Build scoring rubrics concurrently with task design (not post-hoc)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Validate each task against actual job performance data",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Plan ongoing maintenance (tools and duties evolve)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Scoring must accommodate alternative solution paths (multiple valid command sequences achieving the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "same correct outcome). Partial-credit rubrics for directionally correct but incomplete solutions.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#4-performance-based-assessment-pba-items",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Psychometrics: Classical Test Theory (CTT) Item Analysis",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Run after every exam administration to flag items for revision or retirement.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#5-psychometrics-classical-test-theory-ctt-item-analysis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Key statistics and interpretation thresholds:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#5-psychometrics-classical-test-theory-ctt-item-analysis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "CTT limitation: all statistics are sample-dependent. The same item's p-value differs across",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#5-psychometrics-classical-test-theory-ctt-item-analysis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "cohorts with different mean ability.[^ctt-sampledev] This drives the migration to IRT for large-scale programs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#5-psychometrics-classical-test-theory-ctt-item-analysis",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Psychometrics: Item Response Theory (IRT)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "IRT models the probability of a correct response as a function of latent ability (θ) and item",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "parameters. The key advantage for credentialing: parameter invariance - item difficulty does",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "not depend on who was tested; person ability does not depend on which items were answered.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Model selection guide:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Key IRT concepts:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Item Characteristic Curve (ICC): plots P(correct) vs. θ; inflection point = b, slope ∝ a, lower asymptote = c",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Item Information Function: I(θ) = a²·P(θ)·Q(θ); items contribute maximum information at θ ≈ b",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Test Information Function (TIF): sum of item information functions; enables assembling forms with maximum precision at the cut score",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Conditional SEM: SEM(θ) = 1/√I(θ); unlike CTT's global SEM, CSEM varies and is typically largest at the cut score - must be reported for pass/fail decision accuracy",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "IRT assumptions to verify:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Unidimensionality (one dominant latent trait; use confirmatory factor analysis)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Local independence (items not correlated after conditioning on θ; case vignette testlets violate this)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Model fit (fit statistics for each item; misfit → revise or remove)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Test equating: when multiple exam forms must be compared fairly, IRT true-score equating with",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "a Non-Equivalent groups with Anchor Test (NEAT) design is the standard. Anchor item drift (items",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "that change difficulty between forms due to exposure or coaching) is the primary equating threat.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pre-equating embeds new items as unscored pilots and calibrates them to the existing scale before",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#6-psychometrics-item-response-theory-irt",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Standard Setting (Cut Score Determination)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Cut scores must be defensible, documented, and tied to a defined performance standard —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"minimally competent candidate.\" The standard-setting study is a separate formal process.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Method comparison:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Standard-setting best practices:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Train panelists on the definition of \"minimally competent\" before ratings (not after)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Run multiple rounds; show panelists inter-rater disagreement statistics and allow discussion",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Document all panelist credentials, training procedures, and final decisions for accreditation",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Apply SEM at the cut score to define a \"borderline zone\" for decision accuracy analysis",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#7-standard-setting-cut-score-determination",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Certification Program Design and Accreditation",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "ANSI/ISO 17024:2012 - The international standard for personnel certification bodies. Key",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "requirements: impartiality (governance separation between certification and training arms),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "documented examination development, reliability and validity evidence, and a competence-based",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "appeal process. Required for programs with international recognition ambitions.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "NCCA Standards (National Commission for Certifying Agencies) - The US-specific accreditation",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "benchmark administered by ICE (Institute for Credentialing Excellence). 21 Standards organized",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "around: governance, JTA, exam development, psychometric soundness, security, candidate policies,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and recertification. NCCA accreditation signals program quality to employers and regulators.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Role separation requirement (both standards): The governance body that awards credentials must",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "be structurally independent from any body that provides preparation or training. Conflict-of-interest",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "management policies must be documented and enforced.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Recertification / Maintenance of Certification (MOC):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "CE-based: earn continuing education credits per cycle (most common)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Point-based: accumulate points across CE, professional activities, contributions",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Re-examination: pass the current exam version at renewal",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice requirements: document ongoing professional activity",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Choice depends on domain velocity - fast-moving technical domains favor re-examination or",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "point-based systems that include currency-of-practice requirements.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#8-certification-program-design-and-accreditation",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Exam Security and Integrity",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Item exposure control:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Sympson-Hetter (SH) procedure: assigns probabilistic exposure caps via simulation; prevents",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "overexposure in CAT; two-stage SH (2023) adds minimum exposure floor to prevent underexposure",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Item bank rotation: partition banks into sub-banks and rotate active pools; most effective for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "multi-timezone global testing",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Field test items (beta items): embedded unscored items that collect psychometric data without",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "affecting candidate score; rotate to operational after calibration",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Online / remote proctoring model comparison:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "AI-resistant assessment design (post-LLM era):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "GPT-4-class models score in the 60th–90th percentile on many MCQ credentialing exams. Knowledge",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "recall items are indefensible without layered countermeasures:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Key threat vectors (PSI Security Guide):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Content harvesting (phone camera while appearing to face forward) - greatest risk",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Proxy testing / deepfake video substitution",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Organized collusion rings across time-zone sittings",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Brain-dump sites and item-memorization services",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#9-exam-security-and-integrity",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "10. Micro-Credentials, Digital Badges, and Open Badges 3.0",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Full certification: comprehensive occupational profile; prerequisites; formal exam; renewal/CE",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Micro-credential: discrete skill cluster; short (weeks–months); stackable toward larger qualifications",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Digital badge: the visual + metadata artifact representing any achievement (micro or full credential)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Open Badges 3.0 (1EdTech, final May–June 2024):[^ob30]",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Each OpenBadgeCredential is issued as a W3C Verifiable Credential (VC Data Model 2.0)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cryptographically signed by the issuer's DID using EdDSA (eddsa-rdfc-2022) or ECDSA (ecdsa-sd-2023)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Badge Connect API: OAuth 2.0-authenticated REST endpoints (getCredentials, getProfile, upsertCredential) for credential portability between any compliant platform and any compliant wallet",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Revocation via BitstringStatusListEntry; expiration status must be displayed by conformant Displayers",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "CLR Standard 2.0 (Comprehensive Learner Record) co-evolved with OB 3.0; bundles multiple credentials as a longitudinal transcript",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "W3C Verifiable Credentials + DIDs:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Issuer signs VC → Holder stores in DID-keyed wallet → Verifier resolves issuer DID, validates signature, checks status - no callback to issuer required",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "DID v1.0 became W3C Recommendation July 2022",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Blockchain anchoring: credential hash written on-chain; hash mismatch = tamper detection; confidential data stays off-chain",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Verification latency: seconds vs. weeks for legacy background check services",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Employer adoption (verified-as-of: 2026-06-16): Tech-sector ecosystems (Google, Amazon, Microsoft) have built badge ecosystems with direct employer metadata consumption. Outside tech, employer recognition remains uneven - standards-based portability is the primary mitigation against platform lock-in.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#10-micro-credentials-digital-badges-and-open-badges-30",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
