          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[^irt-invariance]: Assessment Systems. \"What is Item Response Theory?\" https://assess.com/what-is-item-response-theory/ - IRT parameter invariance; CAT; TIF; pre-equating.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#references",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[^sh-2023]: PubMed. \"Controlling the Minimum Item Exposure Rate in CAT: A Two-Stage Sympson-Hetter Procedure\" (2023). https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37997579/ - Two-stage SH for minimum + maximum exposure control.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#references",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[^llm-resistant]: arXiv 2304.12203. \"Creating Large Language Model Resistant Exams\" (2023). https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.12203 - LLM-resistant item design principles; performance-based countermeasures.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/assessment-certification-design/#references",
          "note": null
        }
